  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UNICEF ASWA III WASH program; Accelerating Climate-Resilient Sanitation and Water for All Phase III</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This top-up of the ASWA III WASH program will be granted for 2026/2027, for Burkina Faso, C&#xf4;te d&apos;Ivoire, Mali, Niger, and Somalia. It allows for an enhanced focus on the Dutch &apos;interest of stability&apos; and resilience and conflict-prevention by means of capacity development and integration of conflict sensitivity and peacebuilding in the program and sector plans and policies. This top-up also promotes further synergy between the WASH ASWA III program and the &apos;No time to Waste&apos; nutrition program in Burkina Faso, Mali and Niger in particular by &apos;co-location&apos; on the community level, for better results and to prevent malnutrition. Service delivery: 140,000 people with basic water services, 330,000 with safe sanitation; also a focus on schools and HCF&apos;s. The program will support nationwide WASH finance strategies (system strengthening). Thematic areas of the global inception report of 2024 (sustainability, climate, women/girls, systems strengthening) remain an overall priority.</narrative>
  </description>
